parameters.text:
=Write a simple, professional offer letter in English for an Indian small business.
Company: YOUR BUSINESS NAME (address: YOUR BUSINESS ADDRESS)
Candidate: {{ $json['Candidate name'] }}
Role: {{ $json.Role }}
Monthly salary (CTC): ₹{{ $json['Monthly salary (₹)'] }}
Joining date: {{ $json['Joining date'] }}
Work location: {{ $json['Work location'] || 'our office' }}
Reporting to: {{ $json['Reporting to'] || 'the owner' }}
Probation: {{ $json['Probation (months)'] || 3 }} months

Sections: date, greeting, offer of the role, salary (exact number above, per month), joining date, location and reporting, probation, working hours 'as per company policy', notice period 'as per company policy', a line asking them to reply to accept, sign-off 'For YOUR BUSINESS NAME, Authorised Signatory'. Use ONLY these facts. No bonuses, benefits, increments or legal clauses that are not given. letter_title like 'Offer Letter – <name> – <role>'. email_body: 3 short lines asking them to read the attached letter and reply to accept.

parameters.jsonSchemaExample:
{
  "letter_title": "Offer Letter – Arjun Reddy – Store Manager",
  "letter_text": "28 October 2026\n\nDear Arjun, ...",
  "subject": "Your offer letter from YOUR BUSINESS NAME",
  "email_body": "Hello Arjun, ..."
}

parameters.jsCode:
const f = $('Offer letter form').item.json;
return { json: { Date: $now.setZone('Asia/Kolkata').toFormat('yyyy-LL-dd'), Name: f['Candidate name'], Email: f['Candidate email'], Role: f.Role,
  Salary: f['Monthly salary (₹)'], Joining: f['Joining date'], Doc: 'https://docs.google.com/document/d/' + $('Create Google Doc').item.json.id, Status: 'draft ready' } };
